\f4\fs26 A chubby, jovial looking chap knocked on the door noting the name, Miles L.3. Security Manager, proudly displayed for all to see. Chuckling quietly and grinning widely he opened the door silently and confidently walked in.\
\'93Who are you? How did you get in here?\'94 Miles, L.3 was far too busy following Mr Hardy\'92s instructions to be disturbed by the fat interloper. \'93I am on important business for Jamison Hardy.\'94 To infer some sort of familiarity and to impress, he dropped the first name of the big-boss. \
\'93Sorry to give you a start, Mr Miles. I have a message from Mr Hardy. He is very impressed with the way you get things done.\'94\
\'93What\'92s the message?\'94\
\'93The message is - Sorry.\'94 He pulled out his old Glock and sent three bullets in tight formation into the centre of the Security Manager\'92s chest and then one into his forehead. Without ceremony, he grabbed the body by one leg and dragged him out to a pile of dead security guards who were unlucky enough to be working that day. These boys and girls would remain on duty, forever vigilant, encased in concrete. \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl360\slmult1\sa160\qc\partightenfactor0

